      "writtenOn": "2025-01-30T07:53:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Doesn\u0027t this just initialize the first element? (If I remember correctly, the rest shall be zero-initialized because we pass some flags to `clang++`. But that\u0027s beyond the scope of standard C++.)\n\nWe could use\n\n    static constexpr std::array\u003cuint8_t, 1024\u003e buffer \u003d []() {\n      std::array\u003cuint8_t, 1024\u003e result;\n      std::fill(result.begin(), result.end(), 0u);\n      return result;\n    }();",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 72,
        "startChar": 46,
        "endLine": 72,
        "endChar": 47
      },
      "revId": "8fe2d5d49574e38ab5b50078969238acb73dbc69",
